.TH TEST-HERE 1 "October 2026" "Noble Factor" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
Test-Here \- run every test under tests/ that macOS and Linux run
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B Test-Here
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Test-Here
runs, from the repository's root, every program under
.I tests/
but the PowerShell ones, each as a program, and fails when any fails, naming each that did.
It points XDG_DATA_HOME at this checkout's
.I Home/common/.local/share
so the tests review its Set-Environment, as on a CI runner that has deployed nothing.
.B make test
runs it; on Windows the PowerShell tests are
.BR Test-Here.ps1 's.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show this manual page and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every test passed.
.TP
.B 1
A test failed; each that did is named.
.TP
.B 64
Usage error \- an argument it does not take.
.TP
.B 72
Critical file missing \- \fBDeclare-BashScript\fR is not in the repository's \fIHome/common/.local/bin\fR, or the repository's root cannot be entered.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
bin/Test-Here
make test
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR Test-OnHosts (1),
.BR make (1)
